"cd /hutian/deliver && git fetch -q origin && git diff 831849a 803e4e9 --stat | tail -5; git diff 831849a 803e4e9 -- paper REPRODUCE.md code results | grep '^[+-]' | grep -v '^+++\\|^---' | cut -c1-1500; forge api repos/world/paper-repo/pulls/29 | python3 -c \"import sys,json;print(json.load(sys.stdin)['head']['sha'])\""]], "output": "```console\n paper/sections/appendix.tex | 2 +-\n paper/sections/results.tex  | 2 +-\n 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n-The interval is $\\hat\\tau\\pm c_\\alpha(\\kappa B/\\mathrm{SE})\\,\\mathrm{SE}_{\\rm HC0}$ at the 90\\% level, with $c_\\alpha(b)$ the $1-\\alpha$ quantile of $|N(b,1)|$, and $B$ one of two bounds on the extrapolation: $B_1$, the range of $\\hat\\tau$ over the five specifications of the ladder (regression, quadratic, spline, count and two-hop), or $B_2=\\tfrac12\\hat M[(1-p)^2+p^2]$, with $\\hat M$ the larger, over the two own-treatment arms, of the largest second derivative of a cubic in $f$ fitted in the arm, over the observed range of $f$ of the draw (noise level 0.5). The multiplier $\\kappa$ was frozen on the original cells before the block ran, as the smallest value of a grid from 0.25 to 64 at which the smooth mechanisms (a), (b), (c), (e), (f) are covered at least 90\\% of the time: $\\hat\\kappa=0.25$ for $B_2$, the floor of the grid, and 1 for $B_1$. At the floor the grid cannot say how much smaller a $\\kappa$ would still cover, so $B_2$ is a bound and not a calibration. On the 666 cells of the block (nine groups: the null column and mechanisms (a)--(h)), $B_2$ covers 0.990 on average over cells (worst group, mechanism (e): 0.949) at a mean width of 8.4, and $B_1$ 0.963 (worst 0.882) at 3.3, against 0.70 for HC0 at a width of 0.68, in units of $\\gate$. The 1296 original cells, which were analysed after the results, give 0.981 at 11.0, 0.945 at 3.1 and 0.67. Where $|{\\rm bias}|/{\\rm SD}>2$ (92 block cells) the coverage is 0.938 for $B_2$, 0.821 for $B_1$ and 0.153 for HC0. The width i\n+The interval is $\\hat\\tau\\pm c_\\alpha(\\kappa B/\\mathrm{SE})\\,\\mathrm{SE}_{\\rm HC0}$ at the 90\\% level, with $c_\\alpha(b)$ the $1-\\alpha$ quantile of $|N(b,1)|$, and $B$ one of two bounds on the extrapolation: $B_1$, the range of $\\hat\\tau$ over the five specifications of the ladder (regression, quadratic, spline, count and two-hop), or $B_2=\\tfrac12\\hat M[(1-p)^2+p^2]$, with $\\hat M$ the larger, over the two own-treatment arms, of the largest second derivative of a cubic in $f$ fitted in the arm, over the observed range of $f$ of the draw (noise level 0.5). The multiplier $\\kappa$ was frozen on the original cells before the block ran, as the smallest value of a grid from 0.25 to 64 at which the smooth mechanisms (a), (b), (c), (e), (f) are covered at least 90\\% of the time: $\\hat\\kappa=0.25$ for $B_2$, the floor of the grid, and 1 for $B_1$. At the floor the grid cannot say how much smaller a $\\kappa$ would still cover, so $B_2$ is a bound and not a calibration. On the 666 cells of the block (mechanisms (a)--(h); the 33 null-column cells are reported separately), $B_2$ covers 0.990 on average over cells (worst mechanism, (e): 0.935) at a mean width of 8.4, and $B_1$ 0.963 (worst 0.853) at 3.3, against 0.70 for HC0 at a width of 0.68, in units of $\\gate$. The 1296 original cells, which were analysed after the results, give 0.981 at 11.0, 0.945 at 3.1 and 0.67. Where $|{\\rm bias}|/{\\rm SD}>2$ (92 block cells) the coverage is 0.938 for $B_2$, 0.821 for $B_1$ and 0.153 for HC0. \n-An interval widened by a bound on the unidentified part \\citep{armstrong2020simple} covers only by being wide: on the 666 block cells it covers 0.99 (HC0 at 90\\%: 0.70) at 8--14 times the width of HC0 (by stratum of $|{\\rm bias}|/{\\rm SD}$), no better than HC0 inflated to the same width (coverage difference $-0.010$, $[-0.020, -0.002]$ over 24 groups). Most of the width is noise in the estimated curvature (7, 25, 110 at $d=5$, 20, 80 with the response removed; true value at most 4.7). Using the true curvature (infeasible) the interval has at most about the oracle's width ($\\kappa=0.25$, the grid floor) and covers 0.91 of the block's smooth cells (uniform inflation: 0.90; the original cells do not reach 0.90) but 0.59 of (b) and (e), whose bias is not curvature; a feasible estimate's cost is not measured (exploratory, Appendix~\\ref{app:extra}). On the t\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "9613e3a2-5127-53ed-9afc-cc2f28e380a0", "at": 1795672877.9549887, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 177250, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "c75f19caae079da1122e491386d7d1a4", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "a7c1e1d2-8c8e-552b-946e-f6a8ee0a0785", "at": 1795672878.0167153, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 177251, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "c75f19caae079da1122e491386d7d1a4", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "0d55d2a4-2d26-5247-9a3a-c462af494da3", "at": 1795672878.0264869, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 177252, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "c75f19caae079da1122e491386d7d1a4", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "40aa52c6-1eba-5d19-a604-58ba06efa569", "at": 1795672878.0821788, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 177254, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentic